WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.037
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.337 --> 00:00:08.688
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.988 --> 00:00:14.961
Unit four: Leisure & Balance. Today you will explain purpose with so that and in order to.

4
00:00:15.261 --> 00:00:17.902
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.867 --> 00:00:22.320
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.183 --> 00:00:24.649
Work-life balance.

7
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:29.124
Work-life balance means a healthy mix of work and free time.

8
00:00:29.717 --> 00:00:32.877
My parents try to keep a good work-life balance.

9
00:00:33.483 --> 00:00:36.600
Your turn. Say: Work-life balance.

10
00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:42.140
Work-life balance.

11
00:00:42.883 --> 00:00:43.745
Downtime.

12
00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:47.260
Downtime means time to rest and relax.

13
00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.466
Everyone needs downtime.

14
00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:52.621
Your turn. Say: Downtime.

15
00:00:55.467 --> 00:00:56.862
Downtime.

16
00:00:57.617 --> 00:00:58.664
Overcommit.

17
00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:02.602
Overcommit means to agree to do too many things.

18
00:01:03.217 --> 00:01:05.773
I overcommitted and felt stressed.

19
00:01:06.383 --> 00:01:09.407
Your turn. Say: Overcommit.

20
00:01:12.267 --> 00:01:13.465
Overcommit.

21
00:01:14.217 --> 00:01:15.148
Burnout.

22
00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:19.624
Burnout means feeling very tired after working too hard.

23
00:01:20.217 --> 00:01:22.286
Too much study can cause burnout.

24
00:01:22.883 --> 00:01:25.234
Your turn. Say: Burnout.

25
00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:28.985
Burnout.

26
00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:30.983
Recreation.

27
00:01:31.983 --> 00:01:34.947
Recreation means activities you do for fun.

28
00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:37.817
Swimming is my favourite recreation.

29
00:01:38.417 --> 00:01:41.382
Your turn. Say: Recreation.

30
00:01:44.233 --> 00:01:45.432
Recreation.

31
00:01:46.183 --> 00:01:47.324
Unplug.

32
00:01:48.317 --> 00:01:52.441
Unplug means to stop using phones and screens for a while.

33
00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:55.235
I unplug every Sunday afternoon.

34
00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:58.119
Your turn. Say: Unplug.

35
00:02:00.967 --> 00:02:02.037
Unplug.

36
00:02:02.783 --> 00:02:04.051
Mindfulness.

37
00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:08.269
Mindfulness means paying calm attention to the present moment.

38
00:02:08.883 --> 00:02:10.987
Mindfulness helps me feel calm.

39
00:02:11.583 --> 00:02:14.073
Your turn. Say: Mindfulness.

40
00:02:16.933 --> 00:02:18.341
Mindfulness.

41
00:02:19.083 --> 00:02:20.642
Self-care routine.

42
00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:26.262
Self-care routine means regular things you do to look after yourself.

43
00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:30.022
My self-care routine includes a walk.

44
00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:33.524
Your turn. Say: Self-care routine.

45
00:02:36.367 --> 00:02:37.960
Self-care routine.

46
00:02:38.717 --> 00:02:39.741
Recharge.

47
00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:43.086
Recharge means to get your energy back.

48
00:02:43.683 --> 00:02:45.811
I recharge by sleeping early.

49
00:02:46.417 --> 00:02:48.872
Your turn. Say: Recharge.

50
00:02:51.733 --> 00:02:52.642
Recharge.

51
00:02:53.383 --> 00:02:54.663
Prioritize.

52
00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:58.718
Prioritize means to decide what is most important.

53
00:02:59.317 --> 00:03:01.792
I prioritize homework before games.

54
00:03:02.383 --> 00:03:05.570
Your turn. Say: Prioritize.

55
00:03:08.433 --> 00:03:09.690
Prioritize.

56
00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:11.416
Boundary.

57
00:03:12.417 --> 00:03:15.612
Boundary means a limit you set to protect your time or feelings.

58
00:03:16.217 --> 00:03:18.948
I set a boundary: no phone after ten.

59
00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:22.179
Your turn. Say: Boundary.

60
00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:25.930
Boundary.

61
00:03:26.683 --> 00:03:27.661
Wellbeing.

62
00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:31.044
Wellbeing means feeling healthy and happy.

63
00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:33.510
Rest is good for your wellbeing.

64
00:03:34.117 --> 00:03:36.630
Your turn. Say: Wellbeing.

65
00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:40.561
Wellbeing.

66
00:03:41.367 --> 00:03:44.750
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:45.617 --> 00:03:48.443
Visal, you look tired. Are you okay?

68
00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:53.918
I overcommitted this week: clubs, homework and football.

69
00:03:55.017 --> 00:03:57.692
Be careful of burnout. How do you rest?

70
00:03:58.783 --> 00:04:01.236
I unplug in order to recharge.

71
00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:04.503
Good. Do you set boundaries?

72
00:04:05.617 --> 00:04:09.848
Yes. I stop studying at nine so that I can sleep well.

73
00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.918
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:13.783 --> 00:04:16.816
Grammar focus: so that and in order to.

75
00:04:17.116 --> 00:04:18.408
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:19.117 --> 00:04:21.360
I set boundaries so that I can rest.

77
00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:24.284
I unplug in order to recharge.

78
00:04:25.183 --> 00:04:27.717
She walks every day so that she can relax.

79
00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:34.549
Both show purpose. 'In order to' + verb. 'So that' + a full sentence, often with 'can'.

80
00:04:35.283 --> 00:04:38.830
Be careful! Don't say: I unplug so that recharge.

81
00:04:40.767 --> 00:04:43.498
Say: I unplug in order to recharge.

82
00:04:43.798 --> 00:04:47.576
'So that' needs a full sentence. Use 'in order to' + verb.

83
00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:51.007
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.196
Finding My Balance.

85
00:04:53.496 --> 00:04:56.029
It's important to unplug and avoid burnout.

86
00:04:57.033 --> 00:05:00.089
Last term, I overcommitted and had no downtime.

87
00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:04.586
Now I prioritize and set boundaries so that I can rest.

88
00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:08.470
I practise mindfulness in order to recharge.

89
00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:13.753
My self-care routine protects my wellbeing and work-life balance.

90
00:05:14.867 --> 00:05:18.392
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:21.099
I unplug blank recharge.

92
00:05:21.399 --> 00:05:25.145
A, in order to. B, so that. C, because.

93
00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:30.804
The answer is A: in order to.

94
00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:35.215
Feeling very tired after working too hard is blank.

95
00:05:35.515 --> 00:05:39.134
A, burnout. B, downtime. C, recreation.

96
00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:44.409
The answer is A: burnout.

97
00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:48.200
To decide what is most important is to blank.

98
00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:52.397
A, prioritize. B, overcommit. C, unplug.

99
00:05:55.933 --> 00:05:58.235
The answer is A: prioritize.

100
00:05:59.433 --> 00:06:02.504
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:05.524
How do you balance study, hobbies, and rest?

102
00:06:14.317 --> 00:06:15.805
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:16.105 --> 00:06:24.377
I study after school, then I play football in order to relax. I stop using my phone at nine so that I can sleep well.

104
00:06:24.677 --> 00:06:26.351
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:31.748
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and so that and in order to.

106
00:06:32.048 --> 00:06:36.825
Today's value is balance. Enjoy screens a little, then play and read too.

107
00:06:37.125 --> 00:06:39.662
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

108
00:06:39.962 --> 00:06:42.927
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

